WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:04.890
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.190
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.490
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:08.730
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:12.550
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:19.530
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.690
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

8
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:25.650
Hi, everyone.
大家好。

9
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:26.730
Hey, guys.
嘿，伙计们。

10
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:27.890
What's up, Ange?
怎么了，安吉？

11
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.990
What's up with you and your cute pants?
你和你那条可爱的裤子是怎么回事？

12
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.690
Thank you for saying that.
谢谢你的夸奖。

13
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.030
I noticed them right away.
我一眼就注意到了。

14
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:33.950
Here's the thing.
是这样的。

15
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.030
I hit a wall with sweatpants.
我穿运动裤穿腻了。

16
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.030
What?
什么？

17
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:37.750
I know.
我知道。

18
00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.830
Guys, one of the reasons we started this podcast was because I wanted a job I could do in sweatpants.
伙计们，我们开始做这个播客的原因之一，就是我想找一份可以穿着运动裤做的工作。

19
00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:45.590
You know, we talked about that a lot early on.
你知道，我们早先经常谈论这个。

20
00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:45.890
Yeah.
是啊。

21
00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:52.090
Well, I counted after 409 days of wearing sweatpants.
嗯，我算了一下，穿了409天的运动裤之后。

22
00:00:52.850 --> 00:01:00.510
I mean, not every single day, but for the most part, for the last 409 days, I would get out of bed and put on sweatpants.
我是说，不是每一天，但大部分时间，在过去的409天里，我起床后就会穿上运动裤。

23
00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:00.830
Right.
没错。

24
00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:05.990
I actually had several pairs of pants that were made of the same material as my sheets.
我其实有几条裤子，材质和我床单的一模一样。

25
00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:07.830
Like a jersey.
就像针织面料。

26
00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.310
They're bamboo.
是竹纤维的。

27
00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:10.110
Okay.
好吧。

28
00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.810
Made by the same company that makes my sheets.
和做我床单的是同一家公司生产的。

29
00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.470
Listen, if I could have pants made by people that make bedding.
听着，如果我能穿上由做床上用品的人做的裤子。

30
00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:17.950
That's what I thought.
我当时就是这么想的。

31
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.630
It's like I'm just wearing my bed around all day.
就像我整天把床穿在身上一样。

32
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.850
I thought I'd hit the jackpot.
我以为我中大奖了。

33
00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:23.130
Okay.
好吧。

34
00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:29.850
So after 409 days of this, I hit a wall and I was like, I need to wear pants, actual pants.
所以在这样过了409天后，我腻了，我想，我得穿裤子，真正的裤子。

35
00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.530
So I went out and I bought a pair of pants.
所以我出去买了一条裤子。

36
00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:33.570
Angela, I'm going to stand up.
安吉拉，我要站起来了。

37
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:34.270
I'm going to show you.
我要展示给你看。

38
00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:35.470
I'm going to describe them to you.
我要向你描述一下它们。

39
00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:36.310
I'm going to take a picture.
我要拍张照片。

40
00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:41.650
They kind of look like camouflage, but like very sassy cargo kind of pants.
它们看起来有点像迷彩裤，但又像是那种非常时髦的工装裤。

41
00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:42.010
Yeah.
是啊。

42
00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.370
That's what I was going for.
我追求的就是这种风格。

43
00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:44.810
Sassy cargo.
时髦工装风。

44
00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:45.250
Yeah.
没错。

45
00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.430
I love a sassy cargo.
我喜欢时髦的工装裤。

46
00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:47.510
All right.
好吧。

47
00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:48.990
So here's the thing.
所以问题来了。

48
00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.650
I think I'm so used to wearing sweatpants.
我想我已经太习惯穿运动裤了。

49
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:54.470
I'm in the dressing room and I don't know which size of pants to buy.
我在试衣间里，不知道该买什么尺码的裤子。

50
00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:56.510
Because you've been wearing the baggy britches.
因为你一直穿着宽松的裤子。

51
00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.350
That's right.
没错。

52
00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:01.390
I went back and forth and back and forth and I went with the bigger size.
我纠结来纠结去，最后还是选了大号。

53
00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.750
And now I've been wearing them for what?
现在我穿了多久了？

54
00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:06.050
I don't know, an hour?
不知道，一个小时？

55
00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:07.930
Now they're all stretched out.
现在它们全被撑大了。

56
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:08.710
They're too big.
太大了。

57
00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:09.590
And look what happens.
你看结果怎么样。

58
00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:13.010
Now they're falling down and I've got long crotch.
现在裤子往下掉，裤裆都垂下来了。

59
00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.290
Long crotch, ladies.
裤裆垂下来了，女士们。

60
00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:14.830
Oh, I see it.
噢，我看到了。

61
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:15.970
You have long crotch.
你的裤裆确实垂下来了。

62
00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.750
Gals, you know what we're talking about.
姑娘们，你们懂我们在说什么。

63
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:18.950
What do I do?
我该怎么办？

64
00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:23.750
When like the seam of your pants is like halfway between your thigh and your knees, that's long crotch.
当你的裤缝垂到大腿和膝盖中间时，那就是裤裆垂下来了。

65
00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:24.830
So what do I do?
所以我该怎么办？

66
00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:25.590
I've worn them.
我已经穿过了。

67
00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.150
I can't take them back and get the smaller size.
我没法退货换小号了。

68
00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:31.010
I think I could get someone to alter it in the back.
我想我可以找人把后面改小。

69
00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:32.970
My mom could do that in two seconds.
我妈两秒钟就能搞定。

70
00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:36.850
And the thing is, is I just, I'm trying to reenter.
问题是，我只是，我正试着重新融入。

71
00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.870
You're trying to reenter the world.
你正试着重新融入这个世界。

72
00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:42.030
You know, I like the sassy cargo minus the long crotch.
你知道，我喜欢那种时髦的工装裤，但不想要垂裤裆。

73
00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.790
What are we doing today?
我们今天要做什么？

74
00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:44.690
All right.
好的。

75
00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:45.510
Let me tell you.
让我来告诉你。

76
00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:48.010
For those of you guys wanting to know what we're doing today.
对于那些想知道我们今天要做什么的人。

77
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:52.390
It is Business Ethics Season 5, Episode 3.
今天是《办公室》第五季第三集《商业道德》。

78
00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:53.290
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

79
00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:57.710
It is written by Ryan Coe and directed by Jeffrey Blitz.
编剧是瑞安·科，导演是杰弗里·布里茨。

80
00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:58.690
Love it.
太棒了。

81
00:02:58.790 --> 00:02:59.890
Here is a summary.
这是剧情梗概。

82
00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:05.070
Jim reluctantly reveals him and Pam's engagement to the office.
吉姆不情愿地向办公室公开了他和帕姆订婚的消息。

83
00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:05.850
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

84
00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:06.230
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

85
00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:06.970
We'll discuss.
我们待会儿讨论。

86
00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:14.430
Following Ryan's recent actions, corporate has required Holly to conduct a seminar on business
由于瑞安最近的行为，公司要求霍莉举办一场关于商业道德的研讨会。

87
00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.070
ethics.
道德。

88
00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:20.610
Michael offers immunity to anyone willing to confess to dishonesty at work.
迈克尔向任何愿意承认在工作中不诚实的人提供豁免权。

89
00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.750
What are we, like an episode of Survivor?
我们这是在演《幸存者》吗？

90
00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:23.170
I know.
我知道。

91
00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.090
You get immunity.
你获得豁免权。

92
00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.450
Everything you say.
你说的一切。

93
00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.450
And then we're going to light the torch for you.
然后我们要为你点燃火炬。

94
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:33.950
Well, some things are revealed, again, we will discuss, and it's going to cause a rift
总之，有些事情被揭露了，我们待会儿会讨论，这会在迈克尔和霍莉之间造成裂痕。

95
00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.270
between Michael and Holly.
裂痕。

96
00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:35.830
Yeah.
没错。

97
00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:42.790
Meanwhile, Jim makes Dwight observe the company's time theft policy, and Meredith provides Outback
与此同时，吉姆让德怀特遵守公司的工时窃取政策，梅雷迪思为整个办公室提供了澳拜客牛排馆的外卖。

98
00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:45.430
Steakhouse takeout to the entire office.
这就是我们的剧情梗概。

99
00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.270
So that's our summary.
所以这就是我们的梗概。

100
00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.870
Would you like fast fact number one?
你想要第一个冷知识吗？

101
00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:51.690
I really would.
我真的会。

102
00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:52.510
All right.
好吧。

103
00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:53.890
New writer alert.
新编剧预警。

104
00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:54.550
Oh.
哦。

105
00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:57.770
Writer Ryan Coe has joined the staff for season five.
编剧瑞安·科伊加入了第五季的制作团队。

106
00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:58.450
Hello, Ryan.
你好，瑞安。

107
00:03:58.590 --> 00:03:58.850
Welcome.
欢迎。

108
00:03:59.070 --> 00:03:59.430
Hello, Ryan.
你好，瑞安。

109
00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:03.890
He was only with us for one season as he left to work on Cougar Town.
他只和我们合作了一季，因为他后来去参与《熟女镇》的制作了。

110
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.310
Oh, we knew lots of folks on Cougar Town.
哦，我们认识《熟女镇》里的很多人。

111
00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.530
We sure did, Busy Phillips.
我们确实认识，比如比茜·菲利普斯。

112
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:08.130
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

113
00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:11.830
He is also a writer and co-executive producer of The Simpsons.
他同时也是《辛普森一家》的编剧和联合执行制片人。

114
00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:12.870
Welcome, Ryan.
欢迎你，瑞安。

115
00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:13.630
Welcome.
欢迎。

116
00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.850
Fast fact number two, no Pam.
速报二，没有帕姆。

117
00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:22.730
Outside of the cold open, where you hear Pam's voice, there is no Pam in this episode.
除了开头能听到帕姆声音的冷开场外，这一集里没有帕姆。

118
00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.250
But there was Pam.
但其实是有帕姆的。

119
00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.970
There was, you guys.
确实有，伙计们。

120
00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:27.630
There was.
确实有。

121
00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:31.410
I filmed a bunch of scenes at art school, and they all got cut out.
我拍了很多在艺术学校的戏份，但都被剪掉了。

122
00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:32.050
I know.
我知道。

123
00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.330
I saw in the deleted scenes, there's like three.
我在删减片段里看到了，大概有三场。

124
00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.790
Well, I'm going to talk about them as we break down this episode.
好吧，我会在解析这一集的时候提到它们。

125
00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:41.830
On Office Ladies, Pam will be inserted into this episode again.
在《办公室女士》节目里，帕姆会再次被“植入”到这一集里。

126
00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.250
She will live again.
她会重获新生。

127
00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:44.330
She will.
她会的。

128
00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:49.770
And also, Jenna, there was an amazing Ryan Kevin runner that got deleted for time.
还有，珍娜，有一个很棒的瑞安和凯文的连贯笑话因为时长被剪掉了。

129
00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:50.530
And it's great.
而且非常棒。

130
00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:51.570
And I'm going to bring that up.
我会把它提出来的。

131
00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.950
You guys, we're bringing it all back today in business ethics.
伙计们，今天在《商业道德》这一集里，我们要把所有内容都找回来。

132
00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:59.710
Fast fact number three, Amy Ryan.
速报三，艾米·瑞安。

133
00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.850
Holly is here today.
霍莉今天来了。

134
00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:07.330
We interviewed Amy Ryan all about this episode and her time on The Office.
我们采访了艾米·瑞安，聊了关于这一集以及她在《办公室》拍摄期间的经历。

135
00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:08.730
Let's hear it.
让我们来听听吧。

136
00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.610
Amy Ryan, welcome to Office Ladies.
艾米·瑞安，欢迎来到《办公室女士》。

137
00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.330
Hi, Office Ladies.
嗨，《办公室女士》。

138
00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:22.890
I'm so glad to be here and to see your beautiful faces and the interior of your closets.
很高兴能来到这里，见到你们美丽的脸庞，还有你们衣橱的内部。

139
00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:25.070
Yeah, I was going to say, welcome to our closets.
是啊，我正想说，欢迎来到我们的衣橱。

140
00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.110
Amy, it's so good to see you.
艾米，见到你真好。

141
00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:30.810
Holly Flax.
霍莉·弗拉克斯。

142
00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.450
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

143
00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:33.210
Hollis.
霍利斯。

144
00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.030
We found out your name is Hollis.
我们发现你的名字是霍利斯。

145
00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:35.570
Is that right?
是这样吗？

146
00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:37.070
Because it's on your little name placard.
因为你的小名牌上写着这个。

147
00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:37.530
Yes.
是的。

148
00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.050
I don't know if I ever knew that.
我不知道我是否曾经知道这一点。

149
00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:40.870
That's a really good tip.
那真是个很好的提示。

150
00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:43.350
Would you have played the character differently?
如果你早知道的话，你会用不同的方式演绎这个角色吗？

151
00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:44.570
Totally.
绝对是。

152
00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.550
I would have been much more, you know, refined.
我本来会更，你知道，更文雅一点。

153
00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.170
I feel like Hollis is much more refined.
我觉得霍利斯（Hollis）要文雅得多。

154
00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.670
And maybe I would have had an accent.
而且我可能还会带点口音。

155
00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:53.490
Oh.
哦。

156
00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:54.790
I don't know.
我不知道。

157
00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:59.650
I think if your character had been a Supreme Court judge, you might have gone by Hollis.
我想如果你的角色是最高法院法官，你可能就会叫霍利斯了。

158
00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:00.570
Yes.
是的。

159
00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:05.890
But you ended up in HR, and so you went with the less formal Holly, maybe.
但你最后进了人力资源部，所以你可能选了更随意的霍利（Holly）。

160
00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.270
That's correct.
没错。

161
00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:07.970
Yeah.
是啊。

162
00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:13.890
When you run HR, you really want to be more approachable, you know, kind of a, you know,
当你负责人力资源时，你真的会想让人觉得更容易亲近，你知道，就是那种，你知道，

163
00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:15.370
warm, fuzzy character.
温暖、毛茸茸的角色。

164
00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.050
That makes sense.
这说得通。

165
00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:20.650
Holly was a warm, fuzzy character, and we're in love with her.
霍利是个温暖、毛茸茸的角色，我们都爱死她了。

166
